{
  "name": "Old Gerta",
  "conversations": {
    "start": {
      "npcText": "Speak UP. No — closer. Right. You're the museum one. Sixty years I kept this house in bread and not one soul ever asked me a thing about it. Sit, then.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "text": "Tell me your story. From the beginning.",
          "condition": {
            "not": {
              "story": "gertas_story",
              "chapter": "the_dance"
            }
          },
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "dance"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You were telling me about Odo. Go on.",
          "condition": {
            "and": [
              {
                "story": "gertas_story",
                "chapter": "the_dance"
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "story": "gertas_story",
                  "chapter": "the_mill"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "mill"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And after the mill years — what then?",
          "condition": {
            "and": [
              {
                "story": "gertas_story",
                "chapter": "the_mill"
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "story": "gertas_story",
                  "chapter": "the_quiet"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "quiet"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I wrote it all down, Gerta. Every word.",
          "condition": {
            "story": "gertas_story",
            "chapter": "the_quiet"
          },
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "heard"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Wish her a good day.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "leave"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "dance": {
      "npcText": "The fair, then, summer of nineteen. Every boy there danced like he was somebody. Odo stood by the flour cart and told me straight out he couldn't dance a step and wouldn't pretend otherwise. Only honest man at the fair. I married him by winter.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "grant_chapter",
          "item": "gertas_story",
          "chapter": "the_dance"
        }
      ],
      "responses": [
        {
          "text": "Keep listening.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "mill"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "That's enough for today.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "leave"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "mill": {
      "npcText": "Then the mill, and forty years of flour. Children asleep on the sacks while we worked. The flood in the bad year — we lost the ground floor and kept each other. The fire in the drying loft. And bread every single morning, which is a thing nobody thanks you for until it stops.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "grant_chapter",
          "item": "gertas_story",
          "chapter": "the_mill"
        }
      ],
      "responses": [
        {
          "text": "And then? Tell me the rest.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "goToConversation",
              "node": "quiet"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I'll come back for the rest.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "leave"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "quiet": {
      "npcText": "Odo's been gone nine years. The wheel stopped when he did — none of the children wanted the flour life, and I don't blame them. But sixty years happened in this house, child, and when I go they go with me, unless somebody writes them down. So write. A life keeps happening as long as somebody carries it. That's all I know, and I had a good one finding it out.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "grant_chapter",
          "item": "gertas_story",
          "chapter": "the_quiet"
        }
      ],
      "responses": [
        {
          "text": "Thank her for the story.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "leave"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "heard": {
      "npcText": "Hmph. Took sixty years and the museum one to ask. Good. Mind you write it legible.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "text": "Leave her to the good chair.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "leave"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
